    "title": "Iran Airspace Closure: Facts and Implications",
    "text": "• Iran closed its airspace for commercial flights for five hours.\n• The closure occurred amid high tensions with the United States over Iran's crackdown on protests.\n• Iran's airspace is a key East-West route, providing shorter routes between continents.\n• Rerouting around Iran adds time and cost for airlines.\n• International carriers diverted flights north and south around Iran during the closure.\n• Indian airlines, including IndiGo and Air India, were affected.\n• Germany issued a directive cautioning its airlines from entering Iranian airspace.\n• The United States prohibits all US commercial flights from overflying Iran.\n• In June of the previous year, Iran closed its airspace during the war against Israel.\n• In 2020, Iranian air defense shot down Ukraine International Airlines Flight PS752, killing all 176 people on board.\n• The airspace closure occurred as some personnel at a key US military base in Qatar were reportedly advised to evacuate.\n• The US Embassy in Kuwait ordered its personnel to temporarily halt going to multiple military bases.\n• US President Donald Trump signaled that any plan of military intervention might be on pause.",
